{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3291","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3291","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3291\",\"parent_revision\":\"f3c4afa28eb1d9883ce02f79b16e2fd4b4569b99\",\"root_revision\":\"9b0b802fa0172f015485c1b1463e8991177147c5eb425ebc0b19ee2c52d862ee\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSurfaced by the multi-perspective-review quality perspective during `/dh:complete-implementation` for #3268 (QG task T0's nested review, plan Pf0e2e907, MINOR finding on `subagent-contract/SKILL.md:23`).\\n\\nThe `<dispatch_input>` rule added to `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` by #3268's fix (commit 620c6fcc6) gates its self-fetch instruction on: \\\"If your `tools:` list carries `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`, fetch the backlog item yourself...\\\" This phrasing assumes every consuming agent declares an explicit `tools:` frontmatter field naming its available tools.\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` has no `tools:` line in its frontmatter at all \u2014 confirmed by direct read (frontmatter is only `name`, `model`, `skills`). Per this repo's own convention, an agent with no `tools:` field gets implicit full tool access (including `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`), not zero access. Read literally, the rule's condition (\\\"If your tools: list carries...\\\") is ambiguous for `task-worker` specifically: there is no `tools:` list to check for the substring.\\n\\nThis is not a hypothetical edge case \u2014 `task-worker` is exactly the agent `close/start.md` Step 5.6 (also part of #3268's fix) dispatches to self-fetch the item's Acceptance Criteria section, per its own instruction (\\\"the agent has backlog MCP access and fetches the item's Acceptance Criteria section itself\\\"). The rule that's supposed to justify that self-fetch behavior doesn't unambiguously apply, by its own literal wording, to the agent it's meant to cover.\\n\\nNo implementation defect resulted \u2014 task-worker's actual behavior (self-fetching via `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view`) is already correct and unaffected; this is purely a gap in the rule's written condition, not a behavioral bug.\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 whether the fix is broadening the condition wording (e.g., \\\"if you have access to `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`, whether via an explicit `tools:` list or implicit full access when no `tools:` field is present\\\") or something else is a wording/design decision for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3268 \u2014 multi-perspective-review quality perspective, plan Pf0e2e907/Pf807b3cf\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a48d569253ad9539d3ed796894be6cb98fd07e9cffc36fa324ffa9814cd9b008\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABYnNiIA\",\"fields\":{\"followup_to\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"added\":\"2026-08-28\",\"layer\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"source\":\"Not specified\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"language\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"status\":\"needs-grooming\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"stack\":\"\",\"item_type\":\"Docs\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"files\":\"\",\"topic\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\"}}"}